  "source": "https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/947381552",
  "note": "Four longitudinal glazed train sheds rise above the curved platforms at Paddington. The roof retains the two transverse strips, varied vault heights and iron end screens. The track approach has raised platforms, thin canopies, a track fan and open clearance beneath the ironwork. A 24 m sea-level datum aligns the station with standard viewer terrain. Platform and wall heights use the sampled rail apron. The cutout replaces the mapped station and attached canopy, retaining the separate hotel, concourse shops, streets and waterway. Preview places the authored base at the recorded absolute sea-level elevation; local tide and terrain resolution remain host-dependent."
